.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH qsh-server 1  "qsh-server 0.1.0" 
.SH NAME
qsh\-server \- Server side of qsh: the per\-user daemon, and the commands qsh runs over ssh
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBqsh\-server\fR [\fB\-v \fR]... [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
qsh\-server needs no root and no configuration: `qsh HOST` runs `qsh\-server bootstrap` over ssh, which starts the per\-user daemon on demand. The daemon listens on the first port of 60443\-60542 free on both UDP and TCP.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-v\fR
Log more (repeat for more)
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
qsh\-server\-bootstrap(1)
Create a session for the client (run over ssh; request on stdin, reply on stdout)
.TP
qsh\-server\-pipe(1)
Carry a connection over ssh\*(Aqs stdin and stdout (run over ssh by the client)
.TP
qsh\-server\-daemon(1)
Run the per\-user daemon (started on demand by bootstrap otherwise)
.TP
qsh\-server\-status(1)
Show the running daemon and its sessions (JSON)
.TP
qsh\-server\-stop(1)
Stop the running daemon; its sessions end
.TP
qsh\-server\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
.SH EXTRA
Environment: QSH_SERVER_PORTS=FIRST\-LAST sets the port range of daemons started on demand.
.SH VERSION
v0.1.0
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/qsh/control.sock
The daemon's control socket (directory mode 0700;
.I /tmp/qsh\-UID
when XDG_RUNTIME_DIR is unset).
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/qsh/daemon/
The daemon's certificate and key.
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/qsh/daemon.log
The log of a daemon started on demand.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B bootstrap
exits 0 after a success reply, 1 after an error reply, 2 when invoked wrongly.
.B status
exits 3 when no daemon runs. Status 42 is never used: it means
"no qsh-server" to clients.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR qsh (1),
.BR qsh_config (5)
